## OpenInference traces Gemini live interactions and their tool calls

Source: Arize AI / OpenInference — https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/releases/tag/python-openinference-instrumentation-google-genai-v1.6.0
Published: 2026-11-05
Channel: github

OpenInference provides instrumentation that records AI application activity as traces. Its Google GenAI integration now covers live sessions, which exchange data through a persistent WebSocket connection. Previously, those sessions bypassed the methods the instrumentor wrapped and produced no spans. A span is a record of one operation within a trace.

The new implementation first creates an interaction record from user input until the model returns control. Within it, separate records follow model generations and tool calls. A tool request ends the current generation; another generation begins when the model continues. Session identifiers connect successive interactions. Cancelled tools receive a cancellation event, and nonblocking calls can outlast their starting interaction.

The implementation omits audio and video bytes but can record enabled transcriptions and remote media references. Images remain subject to masking settings, and the session-resumption handle is omitted. The contributor reports a real API smoke test with text and tool turns, but no real microphone or Vertex backend test. Tracing also wraps private SDK functions; their removal can reduce coverage, and streamed tool arguments may be incomplete.

Why it matters: Teams observing live Gemini applications gain interaction-level records, but should verify their media, backend and streaming paths rather than assume the reported text smoke test covers them.

